ser wants to bind a pump widget (泵1) on the main page (主画面) to a motor device (马达3). Let me break this down:\n\n1. First, I need to find the main page (主画面) - I should list pages to find it\n2. I need to find the pump1 widget on that page\n3. I need to find the motor device (马达3) - I should list devices to find it\n\nLet me start by listing pages and devices to get the necessary information."}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 26885, "output_tokens": 590, "latency_ms": 15056.198200036306, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "我找到了主画面页面（ID: `main_page`），但目前系统中**没有注册任何设备**，所以\"马达3\"还不存在。\n\n另外，我还需要确认以下信息才能完成绑定：\n\n1. **泵1 的 widget ID** — 主画面上的泵控件叫什么 ID？\n2. **马达3 对应的 SCADA 点位标签（tag）** — 您希望把泵1绑定到哪个点位上？\n\n请问：\n- 您是否需要我先帮您**创建一个马达设备（motor3）**？\n- 或者您是想把泵1绑定到某个已经存在的**SCADA点位**上？请提供点位的 tag 名称。\n\n如果马达3设备和相关点位都还没配置，我可以先帮您注册设备并创建点位，然后再完成绑定。请告诉我您的需求。", "reasoning": "I found the main page (主画面) with ID \"main_page\". However, there are no devices registered in the system yet. \n\nThe user wants to bind \"泵1\" (pump1) on the main page to \"马达3\" (motor3). But:\n1. I don't know the widget_id for 泵1 - I need to check what widgets are on the main page\n2. There are no devices registered, so 马达3 doesn't exist\n\nI need to clarify with the user what they mean by \"绑到马达3上\". Do they want to:\n1. Bind the pump widget to a SCADA point tag associated with motor3?\n2. Or something else?\n\nLet me think about this differently. In SCADA systems, \"binding\" typically means connecting a widget to a data point/tag. The user might mean:\n- There's a widget called \"泵1\" on the main page\n- They want to bind it to a tag related to \"马达3\" (motor 3)\n\nBut I don't have visibility into what widgets exist on the main page or what points/tags exist. Let me ask the user for clarification since:\n1. No devices are registered (so 马达3 doesn't exist in the device catalog)\n2. I don't know the widget ID for 泵1\n3. I need to understand what tag they want to bind to\n\nActually, looking at the bind_point function, it binds a SCADA point tag to a widget property. So the user needs:\n1. A widget on the main page (泵1) - need widget_id\n2. A SCADA point tag to bind to it - the user mentions 马达3\n\nI should inform the user that:\n1. There are no devices registered yet\n2. I need to know what SCADA point tag they want to bind to the pump widget\n\nLet me ask the user for clarification."}], "rag": {"enabled": false, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": false, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 53530, "output_tokens": 750, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 23598.898599972017}, "judge": null}
