"}, {"name": "restore_project"}, {"name": "create_database_table"}, {"name": "configure_database_connection"}, {"name": "execute_sql_query"}, {"name": "set_retention_policy"}, {"name": "list_databases"}, {"name": "create_notification_rule"}, {"name": "configure_notification_channel"}, {"name": "add_escalation_level"}], "visible_count": 100, "selected": "create_analog_alarm", "action": "create_analog_alarm", "args": {"action": "create_analog_alarm", "high_limit": "2.0", "id": "alarm_pump01_pressure_high", "tag": "PUMP_01_PRESSURE"}, "schema_valid": true, "result_ok": false, "error_code": "ALREADY_EXISTS", "error_msg": "alarm alarm_pump01_pressure_high already exists", "result_data": {}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 0.033699965570122004, "intended_entities": ["alarms.alarm_pump01_pressure_high"], "referenced_entities": ["points.PUMP_01_PRESSURE"]}], "resource_reads": [], "world_snapshots": {"initial_hash": "sha256:43d4f3e3424d08e6d0df74e774e92c960d43209e2c18f450ef8c3b2b7ba60734", "final_hash": "sha256:6eafddcdc3dab01fd4791dff365433375036abe2d15c14882cfd0fca4d407525", "final_state_match": null, "match_mode": null, "diff_against_expected": {}}, "llm_calls": [{"turn": 1, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 26653, "output_tokens": 766, "latency_ms": 18092.82489999896, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "好的！我来帮你搭建一个完整的泵站控制台，包括：点位定义、HMI页面、启停控制按钮、状态指示、仪表显示和报警配置。\n\n先创建所需的 SCADA 点位：", "reasoning": "The user wants to create a pump station control console with start/stop controls and alarms. Let me break this down:\n\n1. **Points (Tags)**: I need to create SCADA points for the pump station\n   - A digital point for pump status (running/stopped)\n   - A digital point for pump start command\n   - A digital point for pump stop command\n   - An analog point for pump speed/frequency (if VFD controlled)\n   - Possibly analog points for pressure, flow, temperature\n\n2. **HMI Page**: Create a control console page with:\n   - Pump widget\n   - Start/Stop buttons\n   - Status indicators\n   - Maybe some gauges for analog values\n\n3. **Alarms**: Create alarms for:\n   - Pump fault/alarm (digital)\n   - High/Low pressure (analog)\n   - High temperature (analog)\n\n4. **Bind points to widgets**: Connect the SCADA points to the visual elements\n\nLet me start by creating the necessary points first, then the page, then widgets, then alarms, and finally bind everything together.\n\nFor a pump station, typical tags would be:\n- PUMP_01_STATUS (digital) - whether pump is running\n- PUMP_01_CMD (digital) - start/stop command\n- PUMP_01_FAULT (digital) - fault status\n- PUMP_01_PRESSURE (analog) - discharge pressure\n- PUMP_01_FLOW (analog) - flow rate\n- PUMP_01_TEMP (analog) - motor temperature\n\nI'll create all the points first, then the HMI page, then widgets, then alarms, and bind everything."}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 27607, "output_tokens": 103, "latency_ms": 3816.0509999725036, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "点位全部创建成功！现在创建 HMI 控制台页面和控件：", "reasoning": "All points created successfully. Now let me create the HMI page and the widgets."}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 27746, "output_tokens": 909, "latency_ms": 17631.50040002074, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "页面创建完成！现在添加控件——泵体、启停按钮、状态指示灯、仪表和标签：", "reasoning": "Page created. Now I'll create the widgets on this page. I need:\n1. A pump widget showing the pump status\n2. Start/Stop buttons (can be represented as clickable rectangles)\n3. Status indicator (circle that changes color)\n4. Pressure gauge/indicator\n5. Flow gauge/indicator\n6. Temperature gauge/indicator\n7. Text labels for titles\n8. Decorative elements like pipes (lines)\n\nLet me create all these widgets."}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 29011, "output_tokens": 1101, "latency_ms": 19234.861599979922, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "继续添加启停按钮、状态指示灯和管道连接：", "reasoning": "Good, now let me add the start/stop buttons, status indicator, and pipe connections. Then I'll create the pressure and flow display areas."}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 30613, "output_tokens": 447, "latency_ms": 10922.266800014768, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "控件全部就位！现在绑定点位数据到控件：", "reasoning": "Now I need to bind the SCADA points to the widgets. Let me bind:\n1. PUMP_01_STATUS to pump status\n2. PUMP_01_STATUS to the run indicator color\n3. PUMP_01_FAULT to the fault indicator color\n4. PUMP_01_TEMP to the thermometer\n5. PUMP_01_CMD to the start/stop buttons\n\nThen create alarms for:\n1. PUMP_01_FAULT - digital alarm\n2. PUMP_01_PRESSURE - high/low analog alarm\n3. PUMP_01_TEMP - high analog alarm"}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 31247, "output_tokens": 378, "latency_ms": 7454.878599965014, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "绑定完成！现在配置报警——故障报警、压力高低限报警、温度高报警：", "reasoning": "Good, bindings are set up. Now let me create the alarms:\n1. Digital alarm for PUMP_01_FAULT\n2. Analog alarm for PUMP_01_PRESSURE (high/low)\n3. Analog alarm for PUMP_01_TEMP (high)"}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 31786, "output_tokens": 263, "latency_ms": 7647.8632999933325, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "故障报警创建成功，修正压力和温度报警参数：", "reasoning": "The null values are not being accepted properly. Let me try without specifying the limits I don't need, or use the default values."}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 32179, "output_tokens": 305, "latency_ms": 5809.55800000811, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "It seems the tool is having issues with missing required limits. Let me check the schema - it says both high_limit and low_limit have defaults of null. Let me try setting both to 0 or some number, or maybe I need to pass both."}, {"turn": 9, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 32614, "output_tokens": 301, "latency_ms": 7349.788499996066, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "This is strange. The schema says high_limit and low_limit are optional and can be null. Let me try explicitly passing both limits as numbers for each alarm. Maybe the issue is that I need to provide both limits for all alarms."}, {"turn": 10, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 33045, "output_tokens": 147, "latency_ms": 5254.486599995289, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "This is very odd. The error message says \"low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" but I'm passing a number. Let me try passing it as a float explicitly."}, {"turn": 11, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 33240, "output_tokens": 177, "latency_ms": 4763.765000039712, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "This is very strange. Let me look at the schema again. The parameter type is:\n```json\n\"high_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"High Limit\"}\n```\n\nAnd similarly for low_limit. Maybe the issue is the way I'm formatting the number. Let me try a different approach - maybe just use one limit."}, {"turn": 12, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 33465, "output_tokens": 404, "latency_ms": 11364.036999992095, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "It seems like there's a bug in the tool. It keeps saying \"low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" even when I pass a number. Maybe the issue is that I need to pass all the parameters including the ones with defaults. Let me try a different approach - let me check if maybe the issue is with how the tool is parsing the parameters.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the error, it says \"low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\". This might mean that when low_limit is not provided, the tool is receiving it as a string (possibly \"null\") rather than as null. \n\nLet me try explicitly providing all required parameters. Actually wait - looking at the schema, the required fields are only \"id\" and \"tag\". The high_limit and low_limit have defaults of null. But the error keeps happening.\n\nLet me try to see if there's something I'm missing. The only difference between my successful create_digital_alarm call and the failing create_analog_alarm calls is the addition of high_limit, low_limit, and deadband parameters.\n\nActually, looking at the schema:\n```json\n\"high_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"High Limit\"}\n```\n\nThis should accept a number or null. The error message says \"low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" which suggests it's receiving a string somewhere.\n\nLet me try without specifying any optional parameters at all - just the required ones."}], "rag": {"enabled": false, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": false, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 369206, "output_tokens": 5301, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 120307.56240000483}, "judge": null}
